    "result_text": "The full suite is just the acceptance tests (the other files are an abstract base and a helper). **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied, the server defaults it to its current date, and the field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` accepts it on create and `OwnerDto` returns it.\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the payload omits it (a supplied value is preserved).\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run under hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically in both directions by name/type, and Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, so both acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass.",
